chapter(3,'evs','plants-and-animals-live-together','Plants and Animals Live Together',
 ("Who lives near plants?","Look at a plant or tree near your home. Do you see a bird, a butterfly or an ant on it? Many animals, birds and insects live on and around plants. Today we will find out why, and we will also look at the soil under our feet."),
 [("Animals that live with plants",["Elephants feed on grass, a moth rests on a leaf and a caterpillar chews a leaf. Earthworms live on leaves and in the soil.","A tailorbird sings on a tree, a woodpecker sits on a tree trunk, ants build their nest using leaves, and a colourful stink bug sits on a leaf.","A frog rests on a leaf, a butterfly perches on a leaf, squirrels use tree hollows to hide and rest, and a barbet uses a tree hollow for nesting.","Some of these animals live under the ground too, like earthworms in the soil.","We can ask ourselves which of these animals we have seen, and show with our hands and arms how big or small they are."]),
  ("Why do animals choose to live near plants?",["Animals, birds and insects use different parts of plants for food, shelter and resting.","Camels eat the leaves of plants. Monkeys love eating the fruits of plants.","Birds like owls use hollows in trees to bring up their young ones. Squirrels and crows use twigs from plants to build their nests.","Sunbirds and butterflies drink nectar from different flowers, and tailorbirds stitch the leaves of plants together to build their nests.","Bats and leopards use the branches of trees to rest and for shelter, and caterpillars munch on different leaves for food.","So plants give animals food, a home and a place to rest, and that is why animals live near them."]),
  ("Life in the soil",["Let us stand on the soil next to a plant, with our footwear removed if we are comfortable, and notice the colour of the soil under our feet.","We pick up a little soil and look at it. How does it look and feel? It may be dry, damp, rough, smooth, hard or grainy, and we may find leaves, small stones or insects in it.","We should also smell the soil and remember its smell.","Soil is the topmost layer of the Earth's surface. It is made from rocks broken into tiny pieces, and from old leaves, roots, stems and living and dead animals like insects.","On top of the soil, between the grass and leaves, we may find ants, termites, small beetles and grasshoppers. Some of the creatures in soil are too small to see.","When it rains and the soil is wet, earthworms and millipedes may come out. We may also find more grasses and plants growing.","If we repeat the activity a day after rain, from the same place, we notice differences in look, feel and smell, and soil far from plants is different from soil near plants."]),
  ("After the monsoon",["In the monsoons we find many more plants and animals around. They did not come from nowhere.","Some insects wait inside the soil for the rains and then come out. Seeds of plants can stay in the soil for a long time and sprout when it rains or when they are watered.","That is why we could not see them earlier."]),
  ("Spotting animals near a plant friend",["Standing near our plant friend, we look around and spot different animals. We describe each one in words and note where it was and what it was doing.","For example: a small hopping insect on the grass jumping around, a black bird, red bugs on a rotting fruit, a blue flying insect, ants on leaves, a butterfly on lantana flowers and a garden lizard on a rock.","Watching quietly and carefully helps us notice more."]),
  ("Sounds of birds",["We close our eyes and listen for bird sounds. We can cup our ears with our hands and face the sound to hear it more clearly.","Different birds make different sounds. A pigeon, for example, goes 'gutru gu'. We try making the sounds we heard and write them in a table with the bird name.","We can notice whether we hear more sounds in the early morning, afternoon or evening. If we hear no birds, we can think about why."]),
  ("Let us reflect",["We can discuss the colour and feel of two soil samples and when we collected them.","We can think about which month fresh new leaves appeared on our plant and which animals we noticed near it.","Then we write the names of two animals we saw near plants, their shape, size and colours, and guess why they stayed there."])],
 [("Name three ways animals use plants, with one example each.",[("Food: a camel eats leaves, a monkey eats fruit, a sunbird drinks nectar.","Plants give animals food."),("Shelter: an owl nests in a tree hollow, a tailorbird stitches leaves into a nest.","Plants give animals a home."),("Resting: bats and leopards rest on branches.","Branches give a place to rest.")]),
  ("How would you describe the soil you picked up?",[("Say its colour, and whether it is dry, damp, rough, smooth, hard or grainy.","Use the touch and sight words from the chapter."),("Say whether you found leaves, small stones or insects.","Soil is made of many small things."),("Say what it smells like.","Smell is also a way to observe.")])],
 ("Tell a friend why animals live near plants and what soil is made of.",["Plants give food, shelter and a place to rest","Examples: owl in a tree hollow, caterpillar eating leaves","Soil is the top layer of the Earth made of tiny rock bits, old leaves, roots and tiny animals","Earthworms and ants live in soil"],["Soil is only sand","Animals live near plants for no reason","Soil has nothing living in it"]),
 ["Animals, birds and insects use plants for food, shelter and resting.","Soil is the topmost layer of the Earth, made of tiny rock pieces, old leaves, roots, stems and living and dead animals.","Ants, termites, beetles and grasshoppers live on soil; earthworms and millipedes come out in the rain.","Seeds and some insects wait in the soil for rain.","Different birds make different sounds, which we can listen for."],
 [M("pa-1",1,"What do sunbirds and butterflies drink from flowers?","Nectar",[("Milk","They drink nectar."),("Soil","They do not drink soil."),("Stones","Stones are not food.")],"They drink nectar from different flowers.",None),
  M("pa-2",1,"Which bird stitches leaves to make its nest?","Tailorbird",[("Owl","Owls use tree hollows."),("Crow","Crows use twigs."),("Pigeon","The tailorbird stitches leaves.")],"The tailorbird stitches leaves together.",None),
  M("pa-3",1,"Where do owls bring up their young ones?","In tree hollows",[("In the water","Owls nest in trees."),("In the soil","Owls do not nest in soil."),("On the road","Owls use trees.")],"Birds like owls use hollows in trees.",None),
  F("pa-4",1,"Camels eat the leaves of plants.",True,"Camels eat leaves from plants."),
  M("pa-5",1,"What is soil?","The topmost layer of the Earth's surface",[("A kind of water","Soil is not water."),("A kind of plant","Soil is not a plant."),("A kind of rock only","Soil also has old leaves and roots.")],"Soil is the topmost layer of the Earth.",None),
  M("pa-6",2,"Which of these live in soil and come out in the rain?","Earthworms and millipedes",[("Elephants","Elephants do not live in soil."),("Parrots","Parrots live on trees."),("Camels","Camels live on land, not in soil.")],"When the soil is wet, earthworms and millipedes may appear.",None),
  M("pa-7",2,"Why did we see many more plants and animals in the monsoon?","Seeds and insects wait in the soil and come out with rain",[("They were made by the rain","They were already there."),("They came from the sky","They were in the soil."),("They were not alive before","They were waiting in the soil.")],"Seeds sprout and insects come out when it rains.",None),
  M("pa-8",2,"Which animals use tree branches to rest?","Bats and leopards",[("Earthworms","Earthworms live in soil."),("Fish","Fish live in water."),("Camels","Camels do not climb trees.")],"Bats and leopards rest on branches.",None),
  S("pa-9",2,"Soil is made from rocks broken into tiny ____ along with old leaves and roots.",["pieces","small pieces","tiny pieces"],"Rock breaks into tiny pieces to form soil.",[("flowers","Soil is made of rock pieces, not flowers.")]),
  M("pa-10",3,"A caterpillar munches on leaves. What does the plant give it?","Food",[("Shelter only","The caterpillar eats the leaf."),("A song","Plants do not sing."),("Water only","The leaf is its food.")],"Caterpillars eat the leaves of plants for food.",None),
  F("pa-11",3,"Soil taken from far away from plants is exactly the same as soil near plants.",False,"It may be different in look, feel and smell."),
  M("pa-12",3,"You hear fewer bird sounds. What is a good thing to do?","Think about why and listen again at other times of the day",[("Say there are no birds ever","There may be other reasons."),("Shout at the birds","That scares them."),("Stop listening","Observing again helps.")],"We can listen again in the morning, afternoon and evening.",None)],
 svgs=[("c3-pal-tree","A tree with animals that use it and soil below","How different animals use a tree for food and shelter, and the soil below.")])
